{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902499-lingering-doubts-about-willpower","id":902499,"title":"Lingering doubts about Willpower","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-28T22:56:18-07:00","id":902499,"title":"Lingering doubts about Willpower","content":"My current understanding is that no 2E splats save Demons regain willpower from sleep.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires</b>: There's only a single reference to it in the book, which only explicitly says that Strix don't regain WP from sleep as they don't sleep. Vampires aren't mentioned at all. On the forums, Word of God says that they do NOT gain WP from sleep, to force more focus on touchstones.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves</b>: There is no reference to gaining Willpower from sleep, save one condition that allows it after 4 hours of sleep (a pregnancy condition).<br /> <br /> <b>Mages</b>: The only mention of regaining willpower via sleep is in a single spell, which says that it replicates the effects of a full night's sleep, including regaining WP if applicable. I guess that effect only works on mortals.<br /> <br /> <b>Beasts</b>: There's only a single reference to it, when referring to Unfettered, which says that since they don't need to sleep, they don't regain WP from it. Much like the vampire line above, it's a bizarre callout given that regaining WP from sleep isn't mentioned anywhere else in the book.<br /> <br /> <b>Demons</b>: Refers to 1E corebook regarding rules for willpower, which includes rules for regaining it via sleep.<br /> <br /> My question is as follows: Is the intent with 2E to remove willpower recovery via sleep for creatures that have a Virtue/Vice substitute? If this is the intent, can all of the half-references to the rule stop being a thing? In every single book there's enough info to conclude that the given splat doesn't regain WP this way, but there's also just enough indirect hinting that maybe they were supposed to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T00:33:37-07:00","id":902539,"title":"","content":"Vampires are excluded because they don't actually sleep, they go into a reduced form of torpor called the day-sleep.<br /> <br /> I you're basically a living, breathing thing that would benefit from rest, you do regain WP from a restful night of sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T00:51:06-07:00","id":902543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902499-lingering-doubts-about-willpower?p=902539#post902539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are excluded because they don't actually sleep, they go into a reduced form of torpor called the day-sleep.<br /> <br /> I you're basically a living, breathing thing that would benefit from rest, you do regain WP from a restful night of sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would a player for any of the other gamelines that only purchased their line's core book (which is supposed to be self contained) know that?<br /> Do you have a source within any of the lines themselves (Not CofD core, since the rule there should easily also apply to Kindred, but explicitly doesn't)?<br /> <br /> FWIW, I agree that that's how it should work, I just think it needs to be made explicit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T00:52:36-07:00","id":902544,"title":"","content":"Hasn't there been posts from developers that vampires should regain WP from sleep? I remember someone mentioning that before when it came up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T01:35:59-07:00","id":902564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902499-lingering-doubts-about-willpower?p=902544#post902544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hasn't there been posts from developers that vampires should regain WP from sleep? I remember someone mentioning that before when it came up.</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually weighed in with the exact opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T02:05:57-07:00","id":902579,"title":"","content":"Ah, I just remember this coming up like every 3 or 4 months and couldn't remember the verdict with certainly. Thanks for the correction <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T02:44:36-07:00","id":902590,"title":"","content":"The only splat that is specificly mentioned as not regaining willpower from sleep is vampire and that's words form a dev on the forum.<br /> The base rule in those sort of situation is that unless a rule is overwritten it work as usual. So all other splat do regain WP from sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T02:44:47-07:00","id":902592,"title":"","content":"As someone who didn't have the 1e rules, I actually didn't know that sleep was even meant to restore willpower until Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T02:49:05-07:00","id":902595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902499-lingering-doubts-about-willpower?p=902590#post902590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only splat that is specificly mentioned as not regaining willpower from sleep is vampire and that's words form a dev on the forum.<br /> The base rule in those sort of situation is that unless a rule is overwritten it work as usual. So all other splat do regain WP from sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2E gamelines (except Demon) are self contained. None of them say you get a point of WP for sleeping, but contain all other rules required to play.<br /> <br /> CofD is not in the same 'Universal Core' position that 1E bluebook was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-29-2016, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:36:08-07:00","id":902741,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they could spare a line to remind you of that if they are reproducing stuff like combat section in every corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T15:45:43-07:00","id":903060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902499-lingering-doubts-about-willpower?p=902595#post902595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2E gamelines (except Demon) are self contained. None of them say you get a point of WP for sleeping, but contain all other rules required to play.<br /> <br /> CofD is not in the same 'Universal Core' position that 1E bluebook was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The beginning of the Rules chapter for Werewolf 2nd Ed. says &quot;for more information, system variants, etc.&quot; see the core book and see the God Machine update. Or, see core CofD. I believe the other splats say similar things.<br /> <br /> I think lack of mentioning willpower gain on sleep is just a big oversight on their parts. For example, in the same Werewolf book, at least in the copy I have (not sure if it's been updated since then), they don't mention Charging. They don't mention it either in the version of V:tR 2nd Ed I have. Yet, I think we can all agree that in a game where you will often use your fangs or your claws, the &quot;charge&quot; action can be a big part of combat for those occasional fight scenes when the game gets less abstract and more mechanical. This is an example to me of how not <i>all</i> rules were included in the splats, just the ones for functionality.<br /> <br /> As for vampires specifically not gaining willpower via rest according to forum Word of God, I think that's more a tribute to old WoD where vampires had to spend a point of willpower just to get out of bed in the morning (a bit of an exaggeration, obviously)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11106,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","user":"Captain Shoe","date":". 05-29-2016, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}